{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790728486,"nonce":"eA1K0Lsp5hFEhuqDHBWwvL5D4jM=","title":"The debug native CI suite runs `crates/zyntax_lua/tests/conformance.rs` with Rust's default test concurrency. The `official` and `warm_up::official` tests each treated `official/all.lua` as an independent per-file case, so two copies of the whole official suite ran concurrently after every constituent file was already scheduled separately.","message":"On Apple Silicon debug builds, the two `all.lua` children reached roughly 160-230 MB RSS each and both hit the 480-second per-file timeout. This added about eight minutes of wall time and roughly sixteen core-minutes to the native CI job while producing only the already-listed known failure. Whole-suite ordering remains covered by the release-only `tests/official_suite.rs` cases (`basic_all`, `basic_all_llvm`, and `complete_all`).\n\nExclude `all.lua` from the per-file matrix, retain the dedicated whole-suite coverage, and remove the now-inapplicable per-file known-failure entries.","files":null}]}